Assumptions:
Let n be a natural number.
Let a be a real number.
Let b be a real number.
For all n, define the expression P(n) = ∏_{k=0}^{n} (a^{2^k} + b^{2^k}).
Assume a and b are non-zero real numbers.
Goal:
Determine which of the following is equivalent to P(6) when a = 2 and b = 3:
(A) a^{127} + b^{127}
(B) a^{127} + b^{127} + 2 b^{63} + 3 a^{63}
(C) a^{128} - b^{128}
(D) a^{128} + b^{128}
(E) Show that it is (C) a^{128} - b^{128}.

